title: the mount
pid: 6ba496c5-a624-47f3-8a29-3ab882fac581
body: |2-
  - Grid on firm feet, so the slab’s mass resists key presses.
  - A heavy slab, about 5–10kg, wider than the grid.
  - A damping layer: felt or a folded towel, so the platform doesn’t keep bouncing after a hit.
  - An inner tube, partly inflated.
    The goal is support spread around the slab’s edges.
  - The table, with a scrap of non-slip mat under the tube if things slide.

  The least pressure that never permits the slab to touch the table gives the best isolation.

  PITFALL: A taut cable would carry vibration.
